"P409256247" "Brass Tuesday"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxVillainArc5Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3856545008" "Antikythera Fragment"
// tDetailString :
"P785797265" "While you're keeping the rest of the Antikythera in storage - in case it turns out to be useful someday - you elected to hold onto this small fragment. It serves as a reminder of the events that news organizations have already dubbed...<br><br><color gold>Brass Tuesday</color><br><br>Shortly after Nemesis stole the power of Pandora's Box, Lastri called a meeting of your allies. There, she declared that fighting Nemesis directly, with your forces as they were, would be next to impossible. She suggested forming a truce with Arachnos, combining forces until Nemesis was defeated.<br><br>You and your allies, whom Captain Castillo dubbed 'The Illuminati', fought your way into Grandville, paving the way for you to confront Lord Recluse. You and Recluse struck a temporary truce, and Recluse agreed to lend you a portion of his forces for an attack on the Nemesis army.<br><br>You realized, however, that a direct confrontation with Nemesis wouldn't work by itself. You needed to remove his primary advantage: control over the energy from Pandora's Box. You returned to Harvan's lab with the Antikythera, hoping to find some way of using its connection to Pandora's Box against Nemesis. You discovered a way to use the device in his lab to 'empower' the Antikythera, enabling it to absorb any Pandora energy that wasn't otherwise contained.<br><br>Your efforts were just in time, as Nemesis's full-scale invasion had begun. He sent his greatest creation, the Nemesis Monstrosity, to bring Paragon's defenses to its knees. You intercepted the assault and made use of the Antikythera's new capabilities, and with each automaton you defeated, you gathered more of the power from Pandora's Box.<br><br>With your newfound strength, you faced down the Monstrosity, and destroyed it. However, upon doing so, a massive surge of power was absorbed by the Antikythera. It proved too much, and the Antikythera shattered, allowing all of the energy it had absorbed to dissipate. The mainstay of the Nemesis army, however, had been broken."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LastriTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2533527867" "{Hero.gender=male Sir|Ma'am}, good timing. I was just about to request your presence aboard the Mitscher. I've arranged for a full staff meeting... I believe we need to address this Nemesis problem."
// Answer Text :
"P216924782" "He dies, Lastri. Preferably sooner rather than later."
// Answer Text :
"P1021530179" "Agreed. I'll head there now."
// Page Death Text :
"P1651271687" "Of course, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}. That's certainly within the scope of this project. However, I believe some preliminary work is going to be necessary before we can achieve this goal. Thus why I've taken the liberty of calling a meeting."
// Answer Text :
"P2154413259" "Fine. This had better be good."
// Page Mitscher Text :
"P1385709821" "I'll meet you on board, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LastriMissionTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P42289559" "So, there we have it, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}. I believe it's time for us to call on Lord Recluse.<br><br>I've called in the mainstay of our ground forces, and I've sent word to Captain Mako of our intent. Arachnos will not react well to our presence in Grandville, but I believe that if we can get you inside their headquarters in Spider City, we will be able to parley on even grounds."
// Answer Text :
"P3987645884" "Excellent. Let's get started."
// Answer Text :
"P4172443012" "A bold plan. Will it work?"
// Answer Text :
"P3795411827" "The Illuminati... I'm not sure."
// Page Name Text :
"P1478799208" "I think it's quite appropriate, personally. It fits with most of the work you've done thus far.<br><br>Arachnos has the monopoly on soldiers and weapons in the Isles, but we've proven that brute force isn't the only form of control. The more agents you gather to your cause, the more you can manipulate events to your own advantage... something that Lord Recluse and his unwieldy army will never be able to claim.<br><br><color orange>Lastri gives you a playfully reproachful look.</color><br><br>Besides which, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}... what's in a name? Clearly it's inspiring to your lieutenants. I would advise discretion in this case. You're about to send your allies on an all-out assault on Arachnos HQ. In these cases, morale is a significant concern."
// Answer Text :
"P3775473910" "Very well. Let's begin."
// Page Doubt Text :
"P475747833" "Honestly, {Hero.gender=male sir|ma'am}, I'm not 100% sure. Unfortunately, this appears to be our most favorable option at the moment.<br><br>Nemesis threatens the survival of both Arachnos and our orga- *ahem* and the Illuminati. Without this alliance, I don't forsee much of a future for us."
// Page ClosePage Text :
"P856364347" ""
// Page NotTaskOwner Text :
"P2620207394" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress through dialogue."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - RecluseTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P1661393069" "<color orange>Lord Recluse glares at you venomously. You get the distinct impression that talking with you is just about the last the he wants to be doing right now.</color><br><br>So. {HeroName}.<br><br>I can only assume that Nemesis's recent acquisition of Statesman's power - a power that was rightfully <i><b>mine</b></i> - and the timing of this attack are not mere coincidence. Am I correct?"
// Answer Text :
"P872117234" "You are."
// Answer Text :
"P2345838627" "Let's cut to the chase, Recluse. You hate Nemesis, I hate Nemesis."
// Page Slow Text :
"P792092228" "And I take it that your presence here is not merely the result of a poorly-planned attack on my headquarters. Rather, you have motives somewhat less ambitious - and <i>less suicidal</i> - than an attempt to usurp Arachnos.<br><br>Am I speaking truth here, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P4144993769" "So far."
// Answer Text :
"P1469105879" "I'll let that 'suicidal' comment slide, Recluse. Are you done?"
// Page Slow2 Text :
"P3254513466" "Thus, the only conclusion I can come to is that you desire an alliance. You are in over your head, and you believe that only with the help of Arachnos can you possibly survive.<br><br>Have I grasped this situation correctly, {HeroName}?"
// Answer Text :
"P2424746636" "Not quite. An 'alliance' goes too far. This is merely a 'truce'."
// Page Hostile Text :
"P2648533357" "<color orange>Recluse's fists clench tight. He leans in close to you.</color><br><br>You... DARE...<br><br><color orange>Recluse's eyes flick to Mako for a moment, then back to you. He breathes deeply for a moment before speaking again.</color><br><br>Very well, {HeroName}. Why are you here?"
// Answer Text :
"P3430132302" "I'm here to propose a truce, until Nemesis is no longer a threat."
// Page Truce Text :
"P3885097658" "<color orange>Recluse nods slowly.</color><br><br>Very well. As much as I would enjoy crushing you, {HeroName}, the hubris of this 'Lord Nemesis' goes far above and beyond your transgressions.<br><br>Our conflict shall remain on hold, for now. I shall devote a portion of my forces to coordinate with yours until Nemesis is neutralized.<br><br>Now, if you don't mind, please get out of my sight."

